#!/usr/bin/env bash

lord --verbose << "EOF"

Using the text files and images in the cover/ directory,
I want you to REALLY focus on which letters are vertically
below which in the monospaced layout of the text below,
and which specific unicode characters each letter is,
and relatively how wide each is and which I'm likely
to have placed below or above which due to the history
of the alphabet and which letters evolved from which.

After you've done that, generate me TWO images:
1. One for the top half of the text below.
2. Another for the bottom half.

Get the vertical alignments perfect in your mind
before you start generating the images.

I want two images, both roughly book cover shape,
each containing the totality of all the monospaced
2-dimensional prose and vertical alignment and
specific unicode characters and their shapes.

Two images. Both the same aesthetics and theme.
Both shaped like a book cover. One front. One back.

